---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ComingSoon from '../../components/ComingSoon.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Smart Cameras — Use Case"
  description="Loitering and intrusion detection with timestamps. Define behaviors in plain English instead of retraining object detectors."
  canonicalPath="/use-cases/smart-cameras"
  mdTwin="/use-cases/smart-cameras.md"
>
  <div class="page">
    <a class="back" href="/use-cases">← Use cases</a>
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Smart Cameras / Physical Security</p>
      <h1>Loitering detection that actually works</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Plain-English rules instead of retraining detectors.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content">
      <p>
        Security cameras can detect objects. They cannot understand what those objects are doing.
        Loitering, tailgating, abandoned bags, slip-and-fall events — these require temporal
        scene understanding that object detectors simply cannot provide. Every time the camera
        angle changes, the lighting conditions shift, or a new event type needs to be monitored,
        traditional CV pipelines require retraining. Primate Vision requires a different prompt.
      </p>
      <p>
        Darwin identifies actions and behaviors, not just objects, and delivers the same
        deterministic verdict every time. Define what "suspicious loitering" means in plain
        English. Set a confidence threshold. Receive timestamped alerts with annotated evidence
        clips — the same output format every time, regardless of camera, lighting, or angle.
        No labeling, no retraining, no brittle YOLO pipeline to maintain.
      </p>

      <ComingSoon note="Full smart cameras deployment guide and example rules — coming soon." />
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 128px 24px 192px; }
  .back { font-size: var(--fs-body-sm); color: var(--color-text-muted); display: block; margin-bottom: 64px; }
  .back:hover { color: var(--color-signal); }
  .hero { margin-bottom: 80px; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-footnote);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-signal);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h1); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .lede { font-size: var(--fs-body-lg); color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .content p { font-size: var(--fs-body-lg); line-height: 1.75; color: var(--color-text-primary); opacity: 0.85; margin: 0 0 32px; }
  .content a { color: var(--color-signal); }
  .content a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h2); } .page { padding: 88px 20px 128px; } }
</style>
